  era: "c. 2600 BCE \xB7 Section 2 \xB7 Indus Valley Civilisation \xB7 c. 3300 \u2013 1300 BCE (mature phase c. 2600 \u2013 1900 BCE)"
  title: Dholavira
  text: On Khadir island in the Rann of Kutch, Gujarat, Dholavira was divided into three parts and had remarkable water reservoirs cut into the rock. A large signboard of ten Indus signs was found near a gateway. It is a UNESCO World Heritage Site.
